==English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|la}} {{term|reprobatus|lang=la}}, past participle of {{term|reprobare|lang=la}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|/ˈɹɛpɹəbət/}}

====Adjective====
{{en-adj}}

# {{rare}} [[rejected|Rejected]]; cast off as worthless.
# Rejected by God; [[damned]], [[sinful]].
#* {{RQ:Milton Lost|I}}, ll. 696-7,
#*: Strength and Art are easily out-done / By Spirits '''reprobate'''
# [[immoral|Immoral]], having no religious or principled character.
#: ''The '''reprobate''' criminal sneered at me.''

